// ==WindhawkMod==
// @id              taskbar-pokemon
// @name            Taskbar Pokémon
// @description     A nostalgic pixel-art Pokémon companion (600+ Pokémon across Gen 1 to 5) that lives on your Windows 11 taskbar: wanders, naps, plays with a Pokéball and keeps you company.
// @version         1.0.0
// @author          menino-dev
// @github          https://github.com/menino-dev
// @homepage        https://github.com/menino-dev/taskbar-pokemon
// @license         MIT
// @include         explorer.exe
// @architecture    x86-64
// @compilerOptions -lgdi32 -lshell32 -lwtsapi32 -ladvapi32 -lcomctl32 -lole32 -luuid -lwinmm
// ==/WindhawkMod==

// ==WindhawkModReadme==
/*
# Taskbar Pokémon (Pikachu)

A nostalgic pixel-art Pokémon companion that lives on the Windows 11 taskbar.
Based on Taskbar Cat by viraj-rgb (MIT license).
Pokémon sprite assets from vscode-pokemon by jakobhoeg (MIT license).

![Taskbar Cat](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/viraj-rgb/windhawk-taskbar-cat/8e9fd963225749cad2ba94e514f65df638d40910/art/preview.gif)

An orange pixel-art cat that lives on the Windows 11 taskbar.

The cat has moods. Energy, boredom and a need for attention
drift over time and decide what it does next: strolls, the odd burst of
zoomies, sitting, loafing, and naps when it gets tired (more of them at
night). If you leave the PC for 5 minutes it curls up and sleeps until you
come back.

Playing with it:

- **Hover** over the cat: it purrs, with hearts.
- **Click**: it meows (or wakes up).
- **Double-click**: it rolls over for a belly rub.
- **Drag** it: you pick it up by the scruff; let go and it drops back down.
- **Whizz the cursor** along the taskbar near it: it may crouch, wiggle and pounce.
- **Right-click** for a menu: pet, treat, nap, wake up, move over, "Stay here"
  (it keeps doing everything else but won't wander off; drag it to move it),
  let a butterfly in, or hide it for an hour.

It also notices Windows: it looks up (and sometimes jumps) when a new window
opens, trots over to the taskbar buttons when one flashes, says hello when you unlock
the PC, and hides during fullscreen apps and with an auto-hidden taskbar.

Between all that it grooms, scratches behind its ears, kneads before a nap,
chases its own tail when bored, and stretches and yawns when it wakes up.

Toys: now and then a butterfly flutters along the taskbar and the cat
stalks it (it catches one about a third of the time). Pick "Play with yarn"
from the right-click menu to toss it a ball of yarn; click the ball to send
it rolling, right-click it (or the cat) to put it away. Once in a while the cat leaves you a gift (a toy mouse): click
it to collect it.

When music is playing it sits and bobs along to the beat (it listens to
everything your PC plays, so videos and games count too). Around 8:00 and
19:00 it gets hungry and asks for a treat (right-click, "Give a treat").
It wears a witch hat in late October, a Santa hat in December, and a party
hat on New Year's and on its own birthday. The tooltip shows how old it is ("day 2"); set its birthday in the settings.

It can meow, trill hello and purr out loud: turn on "Sounds" in the settings.
The sounds are generated by the mod itself, and it stays quiet while Do Not
Disturb is on or a fullscreen app is running.

Its mood, spot on the taskbar, age and your gift count are remembered across
restarts.

The cat lives on the main taskbar only (not the taskbars of other monitors),
and only on a horizontal taskbar. Everything
above can be tuned or switched off in the settings.

Empty taskbar space stays click-through, and the cat hides with an
auto-hidden taskbar or a fullscreen app.
*/
// ==/WindhawkModReadme==

